// XFAIL: RT-257: a range index written as a struct literal, an `if`'s arms or a block's tail is typed Range<i32>: "expected 'usize', got 'Range<i32>'" (0.30.2)
// rustc infers usize for each from the index (`&s[Range { start: 3, end:
// 5 }]`, `&s[if b { 3..5 } else { 0..1 }]`, `&s[{ 3..5 }]`) and prints the
// EXPECT line. RT-177c is a `let r = 1..3;` local; these are literals the
// index does not reach. From the review of g302index (forms o02, o03,
// o07); v0.30.1 the same.
// EXPECT: ll ll ll
use std::ops::Range;

fn main() {
    let s = "héllo";
    let b = s.len() > 2;
    let x = &s[Range { start: 3, end: 5 }];
    let y = &s[if b { 3..5 } else { 0..1 }];
    let z = &s[{ 3..5 }];
    println("{} {} {}", x, y, z);
}
